<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Function Notation — solving f(x)=k</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Let \(f(x) = {@fx@}\).</p>
<p>Find the value of \(x\) for which \(f(x) = {@k@}\). Give your answer as an exact value: a whole number or a fraction.</p>
<div>\(x =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>In \(f(x)={@k@}\) the number \({@k@}\) is an <strong>output</strong> of \(f\), and we are asked for the <strong>input</strong> that produces it. So we must <strong>solve</strong> the equation \({@fx@}={@k@}\) for \(x\), not evaluate \(f\) at \(x={@k@}\). Undo the operations of \(f\) in reverse order: first subtract \({@r@}\) from both sides, then divide both sides by \({@p@}\).</p>
\[ {@fx@} = {@k@} \]
\[ {@p*x@} = {@k@}-{@r@} = {@k-r@} \]
\[ x = \dfrac{ {@k-r@} }{ {@p@} } = {@ta@}. \]
<p>Check: \(f({@ta@}) = {@p@}\times {@ta@} + {@r@} = {@k@}\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2026063000</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text><![CDATA[p : rand_with_prohib(2,9,[]);
r : rand_with_prohib(1,9,[]);
k : rand_with_prohib(10,30,[]);
fx : p*x+r;
ta : (k-r)/p;
/* Diagnostics. Both are positive and differ from ta on every seed (r >= 1). The generic test uses ta-100, which is negative, so it cannot hit either. */
wrong_eval : p*k+r;                     /* evaluated f(k) instead of solving f(x)=k */
wrong_sign : (k+r)/p;                   /* added r instead of subtracting it */]]></text>
    </questionvariables>
    <specificfeedback format="html">
